Article 5 (Dismissal from Commission)
The Prime Minister may dismiss a commissioned member from his or her commission if the member falls under any of the following:
1. Where the member becomes unable to perform duties due to physical or mental frailty or other reasons;
2. Where the member has engaged in misconduct in connection with his or her duties;
3. Where the member is deemed unsuitable due to neglect of duties, conduct undermining dignity, or other reasons;
4. Where the member states that he or she finds it difficult to continue performing duties.
